WEBVTT

00:55.973 --> 00:58.809
FILING FOR LOVE

01:01.854 --> 01:02.855
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:02.938 --> 01:04.065
Joo In-a's

01:04.982 --> 01:06.025
having an affair?

01:09.653 --> 01:11.739
HEAD OF AUDIT JOO IN-A

01:12.615 --> 01:14.033
Will you hear me out?

01:14.116 --> 01:16.452
It's really a misunderstanding,
Ms. Joo.

01:16.535 --> 01:18.662
I said no, but the supplier said

01:19.163 --> 01:20.581
it's customary.

01:21.123 --> 01:23.584
Ms. Joo... Come on, Ms. Joo.

01:24.377 --> 01:26.212
Please, listen to me.

01:27.505 --> 01:28.589
Let me off just this once.

01:29.673 --> 01:32.176
My kids are young, and my wife
quit her job to care for them.

01:32.259 --> 01:34.053
I'm all they have right now.

01:34.804 --> 01:36.097
Please, just this one time.

01:37.807 --> 01:40.559
You should've thought of your wife
and kids before taking the kickback.

01:40.935 --> 01:42.770
Don't use them
as a sentimental excuse.

01:43.062 --> 01:44.105
What was that?

01:45.815 --> 01:46.816
Hey, you.

02:02.540 --> 02:03.874
Know your limits.

02:04.458 --> 02:06.961
A cornered mouse can bite the cat.

02:17.221 --> 02:18.222
Darn it!

02:25.479 --> 02:26.730
What are you staring at?

02:29.191 --> 02:31.360
You weren't hoping
I'd get slapped, were you?

02:43.038 --> 02:44.415
She's such a freak.

02:49.003 --> 02:50.546
Joo In-a couldn't possibly be
having an affair.

02:51.172 --> 02:53.257
- It can't be.
- Mr. Noh.

02:57.636 --> 02:58.637
Yes?

03:02.349 --> 03:03.851
I thought you wanted to talk to me.

03:05.186 --> 03:06.187
Oh, well...

03:06.270 --> 03:07.605
All right, for now...

03:08.439 --> 03:11.400
Let's backtrack strategically
until I've grasped the situation.

03:13.444 --> 03:14.778
I wanted to apologize.

03:16.113 --> 03:18.115
I was rude at karaoke yesterday.

03:19.825 --> 03:21.577
I'm really sorry, Ms. Joo.

03:27.875 --> 03:28.918
I get it.

03:29.793 --> 03:32.046
I was a bit indifferent
and insensitive.

03:32.421 --> 03:35.174
I put someone like you
in charge of very limited duties.

03:35.841 --> 03:36.884
You must've been frustrated.

03:38.511 --> 03:39.512
Well...

03:41.555 --> 03:43.474
I'll give you more work.

03:44.767 --> 03:45.809
Sure.

04:00.783 --> 04:02.284
Wait, Mr. Noh.

04:02.910 --> 04:04.119
Why are you doing this?

04:06.997 --> 04:08.040
Oh, dear.

04:08.499 --> 04:10.417
Why did you have to go and...

04:11.460 --> 04:13.212
Why did you take her on?

04:15.881 --> 04:17.967
You really need to be careful.

04:18.050 --> 04:19.468
Seeing how she handled Mr. Seo

04:19.552 --> 04:21.387
made me realize
how she got called "JJCC."

04:21.887 --> 04:24.723
"Jeer Joo, Chaos Comes."

04:24.807 --> 04:26.767
That spells JJCC.

04:26.850 --> 04:28.310
JEER JOO, CHAOS COMES

04:28.394 --> 04:30.187
Gosh, just thinking about it...

04:31.730 --> 04:32.815
Mr. Noh.

04:34.400 --> 04:35.568
I'll leave this here.

04:35.818 --> 04:37.111
Since you're at it.

04:37.194 --> 04:39.280
You know I'm rooting for you, right?

04:39.655 --> 04:40.698
Stay strong.

04:46.495 --> 04:48.038
Jeez...

05:09.351 --> 05:10.436
My gosh.

05:34.209 --> 05:36.629
What the heck?

05:37.504 --> 05:39.131
Darn it all.

05:47.431 --> 05:49.183
JJCC, my foot.

05:50.267 --> 05:53.020
She's just an employee
like everyone else.

05:54.480 --> 05:55.898
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

05:55.981 --> 05:57.232
MS. JOO IN-A IS INVOLVED

05:57.316 --> 05:58.776
IN AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

06:00.736 --> 06:01.987
Yes.

06:02.071 --> 06:05.115
If that report turns out to be true

06:05.949 --> 06:08.535
that means I'll have what I need
to take Joo In-a down.

06:09.953 --> 06:11.038
This could be

06:12.122 --> 06:13.791
my opportunity.

06:16.043 --> 06:17.461
Fine, Joo In-a.

06:18.379 --> 06:19.672
I'll take you on.

06:20.839 --> 06:23.258
Let's see who comes to a grizzly end.

06:37.064 --> 06:39.900
EPISODE 3:
A WOMAN WITH A TWIST

06:45.030 --> 06:46.115
A workplace is a battlefield.

06:47.574 --> 06:50.411
Every single day,
we fight hard to survive and win.

06:52.996 --> 06:54.581
The fundamental rule of war is IFF.

06:55.916 --> 06:57.459
Identifying friend or foe.

07:00.129 --> 07:01.130
However...

07:02.005 --> 07:03.048
Good morning.

07:03.632 --> 07:05.592
Ma'am, you colored your hair.

07:06.009 --> 07:07.636
You look 20 years younger.

07:07.886 --> 07:08.887
Hello.

07:09.596 --> 07:12.683
Sang-hyeon, you drank too much.
Soothe yourself or you'll get sick.

07:12.766 --> 07:15.102
Identifying friend and foe at work

07:15.602 --> 07:16.645
is not at all easy.

07:17.938 --> 07:19.857
Some foes look like friends.

07:20.232 --> 07:21.692
I never see you around.

07:21.775 --> 07:23.026
We should meet up soon.

07:23.444 --> 07:25.988
Your team and mine
could exchange info.

07:26.280 --> 07:27.990
Yes, sure. That would be nice.

07:28.157 --> 07:30.909
Let's meet for a drink another time.

07:30.993 --> 07:31.994
Sounds good.

07:32.870 --> 07:34.037
Yes, take care.

07:36.206 --> 07:38.417
- Oh, my gosh.
- Today's friend

07:39.084 --> 07:40.294
could become tomorrow's foe.

07:40.377 --> 07:42.087
Why are you pushing this on your own?

07:42.171 --> 07:43.380
You just clocked in?

07:43.464 --> 07:45.632
I do this every day.

07:45.716 --> 07:46.842
Even so.

07:46.925 --> 07:48.844
Be careful. You might hurt your back.

07:48.927 --> 07:50.679
Don't you worry about my back.

07:51.180 --> 07:53.640
Pushing this cart takes know-how,
not brute strength.

07:53.724 --> 07:55.517
- You do this.
- Oh, my gosh.

07:57.436 --> 07:59.313
This is almost scientific.

07:59.855 --> 08:01.940
It's nice to have some help.

08:03.317 --> 08:06.820
TEAM LEADER MOO KWANG-IL

08:12.034 --> 08:13.285
But one thing is clear.

08:14.495 --> 08:16.121
The moment you identify a foe

08:16.914 --> 08:18.499
that is exactly what they become.

08:29.718 --> 08:30.719
As of now

08:31.428 --> 08:33.096
I will sharpen my blade quietly

08:33.972 --> 08:35.098
for my archenemy.

08:35.182 --> 08:36.350
NEW FOLDER: NONAME

08:36.433 --> 08:39.311
And plan a critical blow to Joo In-a.

08:42.189 --> 08:43.649
Ms. Joo In-a.

08:44.483 --> 08:47.820
You asked to be excluded
from the executive staff meeting.

08:48.195 --> 08:50.989
Yes, Haemu's Audit Team
is an audit team only in name.

08:51.073 --> 08:52.825
Our tasks are not independent.

08:53.200 --> 08:54.952
We need to renew
our chain of command.

08:55.369 --> 08:58.038
We are fully under the control
of management for now.

08:59.373 --> 09:01.041
That almost hurts to hear.

09:02.417 --> 09:03.836
I can't approve your request.

09:04.878 --> 09:06.213
I would like for you

09:07.589 --> 09:08.882
to be under my control.

09:13.220 --> 09:14.930
Please reconsider my request.

09:16.265 --> 09:18.016
Well, I have a lot of work
to catch up on.

09:18.100 --> 09:19.434
I will excuse myself.

09:28.735 --> 09:30.362
She's as independent
as she needs to be.

09:30.445 --> 09:31.947
Shall I hear from HR next?

09:35.742 --> 09:37.411
Okay, so...

09:37.995 --> 09:39.204
President Jeon wants to reinstate

09:40.455 --> 09:42.916
Managing Director Jeon Sung-yeol
to the head office.

09:43.375 --> 09:46.295
He called me himself this morning.

09:46.378 --> 09:48.422
Yes, I'm aware of that.

09:50.007 --> 09:51.049
You are, right?

09:51.550 --> 09:54.052
I knew you'd be aware
of the situation.

09:54.136 --> 09:55.762
You are the vice president.

09:56.221 --> 10:00.058
Still, you should've run it by me
before bringing this to the meeting.

10:00.392 --> 10:01.393
It's a sensitive matter.

10:03.103 --> 10:04.771
I apologize. That was careless of me.

10:06.481 --> 10:07.858
To be honest, personally

10:08.859 --> 10:11.111
the risk of reinstating
Managing Director Jeon

10:11.403 --> 10:13.864
right after the end
of his probation period

10:14.448 --> 10:16.074
is quite concerning.

10:22.414 --> 10:23.457
Is it the President?

10:29.421 --> 10:30.631
PRESIDENT JEON

10:37.596 --> 10:39.181
Hello, Father. It's Jae-yeol.

10:40.265 --> 10:41.433
Did I call the wrong person?

10:41.516 --> 10:44.561
I apologize. We were in a meeting,
so I answered her phone.

10:44.645 --> 10:45.979
Sign the form.

10:47.105 --> 10:48.148
The thing is...

10:50.943 --> 10:52.402
HR voiced their concern.

10:53.403 --> 10:55.155
It's still a bit early.

10:55.238 --> 10:57.074
Some will criticize us
for putting on a show...

10:57.157 --> 10:58.617
Haven't you seen
Haemu Construction's stocks?

10:58.867 --> 11:00.077
You must acknowledge what's due.

11:00.661 --> 11:01.745
Don't make me repeat myself.

11:18.303 --> 11:21.014
Thanks for working hard today.
See you tomorrow.

11:21.098 --> 11:22.891
- Goodbye.
- Take care.

11:25.185 --> 11:26.561
Who wants to have dinner with me?

11:26.895 --> 11:28.313
My wife wants me to eat out.

11:30.649 --> 11:31.650
No one?

11:32.359 --> 11:34.027
- See you tomorrow.
- Yes, bye.

11:34.111 --> 11:35.362
- Goodbye.
- There's no one.

11:35.654 --> 11:37.656
Are you all trying to lose weight?

11:38.073 --> 11:40.909
Yes, sure. Got it.

11:57.801 --> 11:58.802
RECORDING, REFRAIN FROM TOUCHING

11:59.428 --> 12:01.680
Project No Name,
following the target.

12:34.963 --> 12:36.715
Is she going straight home?

13:27.849 --> 13:30.352
One triangle gimbap, a can of beer

13:31.978 --> 13:33.105
and a box of digestive medicine?

13:38.777 --> 13:40.112
My gosh.

13:43.323 --> 13:44.449
What are you, mister?

13:44.699 --> 13:46.660
Are you a stalker? A beggar?

13:50.789 --> 13:51.832
Did you hear the news?

13:52.082 --> 13:54.042
The VP's stepbrother
Managing Director Jeon Sung-yeol

13:54.126 --> 13:55.418
is coming back here.

13:56.002 --> 13:59.297
They say the president
favors him over the VP.

14:00.173 --> 14:02.676
Is it because
he's the current wife's son?

14:02.759 --> 14:04.094
This is top secret.

14:04.177 --> 14:06.096
The VP's birth mother.

14:06.346 --> 14:09.099
She was basically thrown out
because of a mental illness.

14:09.307 --> 14:11.309
They called her
a disgrace to the family.

14:12.811 --> 14:15.480
There's even talk
that they think it's hereditary.

14:15.564 --> 14:17.274
- Then the VP...
- Come on, now.

14:17.607 --> 14:20.527
Aren't you two too young
to have a prejudice like that?

14:21.570 --> 14:24.364
If Director Jeon does come back

14:24.447 --> 14:27.617
all we have to do
is decide whose side to take.

14:28.034 --> 14:29.244
Wouldn't it be better

14:29.744 --> 14:32.455
to side with the managing director?

14:32.914 --> 14:36.251
The current VP is in charge
only in title.

14:36.334 --> 14:37.502
He doesn't have a stake in Haemu.

14:39.296 --> 14:40.338
Hey, guys.

14:41.631 --> 14:42.674
It's not like that.

14:43.592 --> 14:45.010
You never know.

14:45.093 --> 14:47.888
The VP has an influential wife.

14:48.680 --> 14:50.682
His father-in-law owns Sesan Group.

14:50.765 --> 14:53.476
The President arranged that marriage
because he needed something.

14:53.560 --> 14:55.187
He has to be wary of them.

14:55.270 --> 14:56.354
You're right.

14:56.438 --> 14:58.231
Then we really don't know
what'll happen.

14:58.315 --> 14:59.524
What I can say for sure is

14:59.608 --> 15:03.486
our company is about to see
the biggest storm in history.

15:03.945 --> 15:05.238
You should be careful.

15:10.827 --> 15:12.287
- Hey, Mr. Moo.
- What?

15:12.954 --> 15:14.706
- Come see me.
- What for?

15:14.789 --> 15:16.374
- Follow me.
- Why?

15:18.210 --> 15:19.920
I packed this for you.

15:20.003 --> 15:21.922
- What is this?
- We made them

15:22.172 --> 15:24.925
for the executives,
and there were a lot of leftovers.

15:25.592 --> 15:27.677
Your wife is looking after twins.

15:27.969 --> 15:30.096
She won't have the time
to cook for herself.

15:30.180 --> 15:31.514
Take some home for her.

15:32.265 --> 15:35.518
Gosh, she's going to taste
some fancy food, thanks to you.

15:36.519 --> 15:37.646
My word.

15:37.854 --> 15:39.439
There's one more thing.

15:39.522 --> 15:41.608
It's not much.
Buy your kids some clothes.

15:41.691 --> 15:43.193
My kids have enough clothes.

15:43.276 --> 15:45.237
You gave too much money

15:45.320 --> 15:47.739
when you attended
my father's funeral.

15:48.114 --> 15:50.033
I didn't get to thank you then.
Take the money.

15:50.116 --> 15:51.618
- It's fine. It wasn't much.
- No.

15:51.701 --> 15:53.328
- You don't need to.
- Take it.

15:53.411 --> 15:54.788
- I don't want it.
- Don't say no.

15:54.871 --> 15:56.498
- You need to stop, ma'am.
- Take it.

15:56.581 --> 15:57.832
Don't do that.

15:58.458 --> 15:59.542
- No.
- What's this?

15:59.918 --> 16:01.378
Can you not do this?

16:03.255 --> 16:04.381
What kind of scene is this?

16:08.260 --> 16:09.386
This is insane.

16:09.928 --> 16:11.012
What are they doing out here?

16:35.954 --> 16:38.081
A triangle gimbap and a can of beer.

16:38.748 --> 16:40.333
That's all she buys every time?

16:40.792 --> 16:43.586
Yes, I thought the lady

16:43.670 --> 16:44.921
just had a small appetite.

16:45.380 --> 16:46.798
I see.

16:50.051 --> 16:52.095
Does she not like eating?

16:55.432 --> 16:56.683
Did she ever

16:57.767 --> 16:59.394
come here with a man?

17:00.270 --> 17:02.856
No, I never even saw her
with a woman.

17:02.939 --> 17:04.983
- She's always on her own.
- Is she?

17:08.111 --> 17:10.989
You must be really smart, Rhena.

17:11.072 --> 17:12.449
You remember all the customers.

17:12.532 --> 17:14.743
No, I only remember because it's her.

17:14.826 --> 17:16.619
Because it's her? How come?

17:16.995 --> 17:18.246
She's pretty.

17:18.330 --> 17:20.749
What? She's pretty?
Joo... That woman?

17:20.832 --> 17:21.875
Yes.

17:32.344 --> 17:33.553
Well, I guess.

17:33.636 --> 17:35.597
We all have
different beauty standards.

17:35.972 --> 17:39.184
She must be what you consider pretty.

17:44.564 --> 17:47.067
Hey, do you want another ice cream?

17:47.609 --> 17:48.943
No, buy me wine.

17:52.697 --> 17:54.783
- Rhena, I drove...
- To share with my boyfriend.

17:59.371 --> 18:01.498
Where would the princesses
like to go?

18:03.083 --> 18:04.209
Where shall we go?

18:04.626 --> 18:06.252
- That way.
- That way?

18:06.336 --> 18:07.796
Here we go.

18:09.923 --> 18:11.257
We've reached the ocean.

18:11.341 --> 18:12.342
Where do we go now?

18:13.259 --> 18:14.260
Backward?

18:18.932 --> 18:20.517
Where shall we go now? Which way?

18:21.267 --> 18:22.727
- This way?
- Girls.

18:23.686 --> 18:25.188
It's past your bedtime.

18:25.271 --> 18:27.023
Go and brush your teeth.

18:27.107 --> 18:29.025
Mommy Monster's angry. Get away.

18:29.401 --> 18:30.944
Run away.

18:31.903 --> 18:33.321
Gosh. I feel so hot.

18:33.738 --> 18:37.242
Oh, dear. It's hard work
raising young kids at my age.

18:37.325 --> 18:38.660
Save your energy.

18:39.077 --> 18:41.246
You need to work
until they finish university.

18:41.329 --> 18:42.414
Oh, my gosh.

18:43.039 --> 18:44.833
Oh, dear. My poor knees.

18:46.709 --> 18:47.961
- Honey.
- Yes?

18:48.795 --> 18:51.005
Your cafeteria food is delicious.

18:51.089 --> 18:52.257
Large companies are the best.

18:52.340 --> 18:53.633
- Do you like it?
- Yes.

18:54.050 --> 18:55.927
It tastes even better
because someone else made it.

18:57.262 --> 18:58.388
Take your time.

18:58.471 --> 18:59.722
Can you bring food home
every now and then?

19:00.849 --> 19:01.975
I'll do that.

19:04.060 --> 19:05.520
It's great to see you enjoy it.

19:05.895 --> 19:06.896
Here's some water.

19:14.320 --> 19:15.363
You're home.

19:16.072 --> 19:18.616
You're late. Did you meet someone?

19:19.993 --> 19:21.077
No, I worked late.

19:26.082 --> 19:28.126
Why did you spend so much
at a convenience store?

19:28.209 --> 19:29.252
Oh, that?

19:30.128 --> 19:31.921
The part-timer
bullied me into paying.

19:33.214 --> 19:34.215
Gosh.

19:34.674 --> 19:36.426
Gosh, ten condoms?

19:37.093 --> 19:38.178
What?

19:42.056 --> 19:43.558
Jeez, that kid...

19:43.975 --> 19:45.268
I wonder if her parents know

19:45.560 --> 19:46.936
what she's up to instead of studying.

19:48.146 --> 19:51.024
If they heard, they'd be relieved
that she knows enough

19:51.107 --> 19:52.567
to take precautions.

19:53.735 --> 19:55.945
They must be really in love
if they need ten boxes.

19:58.239 --> 20:00.617
Hey, ten boxes is nothing.

20:01.534 --> 20:04.078
You know... Back in my day...

20:15.298 --> 20:17.592
Is that what you're eating
for dinner?

20:17.884 --> 20:18.968
Why didn't you order takeout?

20:19.052 --> 20:21.471
I had dinner.
This is a late-night snack.

20:23.515 --> 20:25.600
Do you want one?
It was buy one, get one free.

20:33.816 --> 20:36.194
KIMCHI AND SPICY PORK TRIANGLE GIMBAP

20:36.819 --> 20:37.820
Hey.

20:39.572 --> 20:41.115
I know someone

20:41.199 --> 20:43.701
who eats just one triangle gimbap
for dinner every day.

20:45.954 --> 20:47.372
What kind of person would do that?

20:47.455 --> 20:49.040
They must be poor.

20:49.123 --> 20:50.333
No, it's not that.

20:51.543 --> 20:52.919
They make a decent amount.

20:55.380 --> 20:56.381
Then maybe

20:58.007 --> 20:59.509
they just eat to survive.

20:59.968 --> 21:02.929
Some people eat the bare minimum
so they don't die.

21:03.888 --> 21:05.765
They might look like they have a lot

21:06.599 --> 21:08.476
but they feel empty inside.

21:09.477 --> 21:10.478
That's why

21:11.020 --> 21:12.897
they don't feel full
even though they eat.

21:13.606 --> 21:15.858
They don't feel energized
even though they sleep.

21:22.198 --> 21:23.366
Who are you talking about?

21:24.117 --> 21:26.578
It can't be you, seeing you're eating
a late-night snack.

21:32.000 --> 21:33.876
- Hey, Seung-hee.
- A-jeong.

21:34.168 --> 21:35.962
Sorry for calling late at night.

21:36.045 --> 21:37.672
Did you check out
the anonymous bulletin board?

21:37.964 --> 21:40.633
There are endless posts
about the VP and his stepbrother.

21:42.427 --> 21:44.178
GET SOME POPCORN READY
SO DO THEY HAVE DIFFERENT MOMS?

21:44.262 --> 21:46.264
A LEGENDARY SITUATION AT HAEMU
GOODBYE TO J'S SUPPORTERS

21:49.559 --> 21:51.102
Information Team!

21:51.185 --> 21:53.354
Do something about it!

21:53.605 --> 21:56.107
Take down the posts
as soon as they come up.

21:56.399 --> 21:57.984
Or block certain keywords.

21:58.067 --> 21:59.986
Can't you block posts
that say "birth mom"?

22:00.069 --> 22:02.322
That won't stop people
from using other terms.

22:03.239 --> 22:05.033
If we block every post on this topic

22:05.116 --> 22:08.119
they'll complain that HR
is censoring public opinion.

22:08.620 --> 22:11.998
And work.com
can't be controlled or censored.

22:13.708 --> 22:14.959
Be reasonable.

22:15.752 --> 22:17.086
I'm not asking you
to censor anything.

22:18.463 --> 22:19.756
That can't be the only solution.

22:21.924 --> 22:24.177
We each have just one mouth.

22:25.303 --> 22:26.471
Can't you

22:27.096 --> 22:28.765
come up with an idea?

22:34.020 --> 22:35.438
This is driving me insane.

22:37.023 --> 22:38.775
- Sir.
- What?

22:39.359 --> 22:40.526
Can you take a look at this?

22:40.818 --> 22:41.861
What is it?

22:42.904 --> 22:44.614
Someone posted it yesterday.

22:46.282 --> 22:47.992
How about we use this
to our advantage?

22:48.618 --> 22:50.119
It could gain some interest.

22:50.703 --> 22:51.954
"Middle-aged romance"?

22:52.664 --> 22:53.665
Hang on.

22:54.290 --> 22:57.418
I know this jawline from somewhere.

22:59.253 --> 23:00.338
Team Leader Moo?

23:00.630 --> 23:01.923
Hey, Moo...

23:03.257 --> 23:05.468
Good find, Ms. Oh. Can you move over?

23:06.135 --> 23:08.262
Yes, let's put this to good use.

23:08.971 --> 23:11.974
Let's see.
A middle-aged woman. Madam...

23:12.183 --> 23:13.601
How does "Madam Killer" sound?

23:13.893 --> 23:15.061
Well...

23:15.478 --> 23:16.813
- That's a bit...
- Then...

23:17.689 --> 23:20.066
"An audit team leader's affair."

23:20.400 --> 23:21.526
Is that more provocative?

23:21.609 --> 23:23.945
Isn't it a bit much
to reveal his identity?

23:24.028 --> 23:26.406
Revealing his identity
will increase the impact.

23:27.323 --> 23:29.367
You don't have to worry.

23:29.742 --> 23:31.619
This guy's a PNU.

23:32.870 --> 23:34.163
"PNU"?

23:34.247 --> 23:36.749
Yes, it's a term HR uses.

23:40.336 --> 23:42.088
It refers to someone who is useless.

23:42.463 --> 23:44.215
What? That's so mean.

23:44.882 --> 23:46.634
When a printed report has many pages

23:46.968 --> 23:50.430
you can fold the corner like this
so the big bosses can flip easily.

23:50.513 --> 23:51.973
Don't you think they'd appreciate it?

23:52.515 --> 23:53.641
You're so thoughtful.

23:55.727 --> 23:56.978
Are you serious?

23:57.895 --> 23:59.147
- What?
- Never mind.

23:59.689 --> 24:01.482
This is how I became a team leader.

24:01.566 --> 24:03.025
Must be why I'm still a manager.

24:06.404 --> 24:07.905
I think it looks great.

24:13.828 --> 24:17.165
SEARCH HAEMU GROUP: JOO IN-A

24:17.665 --> 24:19.542
JOO IN-A'S PERSONNEL FILE

24:22.670 --> 24:23.671
SEARCH REQUEST FOR LEISURE STIPEND

24:23.755 --> 24:25.715
NO REQUEST FOR LEISURE STIPEND

24:27.425 --> 24:28.593
NO APPROVED REQUEST FOR LEAVE

24:28.676 --> 24:29.719
NO RECORD OF COMPANY CARD USE

24:43.733 --> 24:46.861
She doesn't go on leave
or claim any benefits.

24:46.944 --> 24:48.237
And she doesn't eat much.

24:49.864 --> 24:51.866
What does she live for?

24:56.662 --> 24:57.955
Did I get you?

24:58.039 --> 24:59.624
You almost fell onto your backside.

25:00.374 --> 25:01.626
Is this what gives her joy?

25:02.251 --> 25:03.336
I scored.

25:05.087 --> 25:08.257
Wait, were you the one
looking after this plant?

25:09.008 --> 25:10.176
Oh, yes.

25:10.259 --> 25:12.303
I water it whenever I think of it.

25:12.845 --> 25:15.890
You're surprisingly thoughtful,
Mr. Noh.

25:16.516 --> 25:17.683
It's quite pretty.

25:20.228 --> 25:21.437
It smells, too.

25:33.366 --> 25:34.659
She's pretty.

25:35.284 --> 25:37.954
Well, I guess you can't say
she isn't pretty.

25:39.539 --> 25:40.540
What was that?

25:41.624 --> 25:43.501
I think you just smiled at me.

25:44.502 --> 25:45.711
That's because...

25:46.170 --> 25:48.798
Do I look funny to you, Mr. Noh?

25:48.881 --> 25:50.174
No, it's not that.

25:50.258 --> 25:52.176
I found your prank hilarious.

25:52.260 --> 25:53.511
When you jump-scared me.

25:54.303 --> 25:55.972
The more I think about it,
the funnier it is.

25:57.723 --> 26:00.142
The more I get to know you,
the more I see your humor.

26:02.937 --> 26:04.897
You caught on?

26:06.065 --> 26:07.775
I knew it. You have the wit.

26:08.317 --> 26:10.361
I don't get
why people are afraid of me.

26:10.444 --> 26:12.572
I'm hilarious, aren't I?

26:13.531 --> 26:14.657
You are.

26:14.740 --> 26:16.117
You get my wit.

26:19.370 --> 26:21.372
Oh, my gosh.

26:22.164 --> 26:25.543
My blood sugar must be going low.

26:26.794 --> 26:30.506
Where was Ms. Yoon's snack box?

26:32.341 --> 26:33.384
What's going on?

26:33.467 --> 26:36.262
Ms. Yoon,
The snack box is in here, right?

26:36.637 --> 26:37.763
Your box of snacks

26:38.306 --> 26:39.807
full of candies and chocolates.

26:40.266 --> 26:41.642
The drawer's locked.

26:43.060 --> 26:44.061
Ms. Yoon.

26:44.687 --> 26:46.939
Did you not like
my getting into your snack box?

26:47.773 --> 26:49.901
You should've told me so.

26:50.276 --> 26:53.571
Locking it away is harsh on your part
and embarrassing for me.

26:54.030 --> 26:55.823
I kept dropping hints
that I didn't like it.

26:56.574 --> 26:58.534
You failed to pick up on them.

26:59.911 --> 27:01.162
Oh, dear. I feel bad.

27:01.621 --> 27:03.039
- My gosh.
- What's wrong?

27:05.041 --> 27:07.627
Mr. Moo,
I think you need to see this.

27:10.713 --> 27:12.089
IF THEY DO THIS IN PUBLIC,
THEN IN PRIVATE...

27:12.173 --> 27:13.174
OH, MY GOSH! SPARE ME!

27:15.092 --> 27:18.012
Wow, you're the talk of the town.

27:22.767 --> 27:23.768
MADAM KILLER IS HILARIOUS

27:23.851 --> 27:25.895
"The Madam Killer"? Goodness.

27:25.978 --> 27:27.480
You're a killer, too, Mr. Moo?

27:27.563 --> 27:29.774
I had a nickname similar to that.

27:29.857 --> 27:31.317
It's not at all like that.

27:31.400 --> 27:33.861
Why would I go around killing ladies?

27:34.195 --> 27:38.407
The photo was taken at an angle
that made us look suspicious.

27:38.741 --> 27:39.784
We were...

27:40.284 --> 27:43.204
That lady and I don't have
any kind of relationship.

27:44.330 --> 27:49.001
I can't believe that smoke
sometimes does appear without a fire.

27:49.210 --> 27:52.630
This isn't just some smoke.
The blaze could take us all down.

27:55.257 --> 27:56.384
Assistant Manager Ahn Min-su.

27:56.592 --> 27:57.885
Yes, Ms. Joo?

28:03.307 --> 28:05.518
I need you to look into this.

28:05.851 --> 28:08.062
Mr. Noh usually takes the PM cases

28:08.145 --> 28:10.064
but that would be inappropriate
as they're teammates.

28:10.481 --> 28:12.233
Pardon? Whose case am I taking on?

28:12.566 --> 28:14.026
Mr. Moo's case.

28:14.652 --> 28:15.653
- Gosh...
- Wait.

28:16.779 --> 28:18.280
Are you going to investigate this?

28:18.364 --> 28:19.573
Of course, I must.

28:19.657 --> 28:21.951
The case is big enough
that everyone's talking about it.

28:22.034 --> 28:24.578
Ms. Joo. It's just a random incident.

28:24.662 --> 28:26.080
It can't even be called a case.

28:26.163 --> 28:28.499
I'm innocent. You know what I'm like.

28:28.582 --> 28:29.667
Yes, Mr. Moo.

28:29.750 --> 28:32.003
That's all you have to say
when you're interviewed.

28:32.795 --> 28:35.339
Drop everything you were working on
until the case is concluded.

28:35.673 --> 28:37.299
If anything needs to be approved...

28:38.009 --> 28:39.635
Manager Cha Sung-tae,
that's your duty now.

28:41.846 --> 28:42.847
That's all.

28:53.816 --> 28:55.860
Why are you still here?
You're dismissed.

28:56.944 --> 28:58.904
Oh, dear. It really isn't anything.

28:59.989 --> 29:01.449
It's really nothing.

29:02.992 --> 29:04.035
My goodness...

29:30.936 --> 29:32.938
WRITTEN STATEMENT

29:51.373 --> 29:52.833
I'm home.

29:57.254 --> 29:58.255
Is everyone in bed?

30:00.216 --> 30:01.258
Are the girls asleep?

30:06.931 --> 30:10.851
OUR AUDIT TEAM LEADER'S CHEATING

30:11.602 --> 30:13.062
They say this is you.

30:13.687 --> 30:14.688
Yes.

30:17.525 --> 30:18.651
The food

30:19.735 --> 30:21.445
you brought me last night.

30:22.696 --> 30:23.948
Did she give it to you?

30:26.992 --> 30:29.370
- Did she?
- No, it's not like that.

30:31.122 --> 30:32.832
How should I explain?

30:44.301 --> 30:46.137
Based on how she treated Mr. Moo

30:46.470 --> 30:48.430
she wouldn't do anything.
wrong or immoral

30:52.101 --> 30:53.561
Am I wasting my time?

31:00.401 --> 31:02.153
Hang on. She's not going home?

31:03.070 --> 31:04.155
Darn it.

32:18.812 --> 32:20.856
Okay. This is it.

32:38.165 --> 32:40.084
SEON DRAWING CLASS,
RECREATIONAL CLASS FOR ADULTS

32:40.167 --> 32:41.335
"Recreational art"?

32:45.256 --> 32:46.257
Excuse me.

32:47.132 --> 32:48.425
Are you going inside?

32:49.301 --> 32:50.928
No, sorry.

32:58.978 --> 33:00.980
Was drawing her hobby?

33:11.323 --> 33:13.367
- Hello.
- Morning.

33:17.204 --> 33:18.539
Oh, my goodness!

33:18.956 --> 33:20.332
Mr. Moo!

33:20.958 --> 33:22.376
Oh, dear. My bad.

33:22.668 --> 33:23.961
My gosh.

33:24.545 --> 33:25.587
Goodness me.

33:27.464 --> 33:29.383
Oh, dear.

33:37.474 --> 33:39.935
Did you spend the night here?

33:40.311 --> 33:42.104
Did you argue
with your wife last night?

33:42.187 --> 33:44.398
Why sleep here
when we have a night duty room?

33:44.481 --> 33:46.400
What are you doing here, Mr. Moo?

33:46.483 --> 33:47.901
Good morning, Ms. Joo.

33:48.110 --> 33:51.363
Something came up,
and I couldn't go home last night.

33:51.613 --> 33:53.949
I couldn't think
of anywhere else to go.

33:54.033 --> 33:55.951
So you decided to come to the office?

33:58.829 --> 34:01.498
You don't seem to know
where to draw the line.

34:02.124 --> 34:05.127
You take cafeteria food home
and come here to sleep at night.

34:09.089 --> 34:10.090
Please leave

34:10.841 --> 34:11.842
immediately.

34:12.384 --> 34:13.719
- Sorry?
- The subject of investigation

34:13.802 --> 34:16.388
does not have free access
to the office while it's ongoing.

34:16.930 --> 34:19.266
This was far too careless of you
as the head of an audit team.

34:20.309 --> 34:21.393
Ms. Pyun.

34:21.685 --> 34:24.271
Request a restriction of his access
to General Affairs.

34:25.397 --> 34:28.400
- Do we have to go that far...
- Going that far is our ground rule.

34:30.069 --> 34:31.945
And Audit Teams are here
to strictly abide by the rules.

34:32.654 --> 34:33.697
Yes, of course.

34:34.156 --> 34:36.825
I should've thought this through.
I'll leave right away.

34:37.826 --> 34:39.036
Goodness, I'm sorry.

34:39.745 --> 34:41.246
Please let me just get my shoes.

34:42.289 --> 34:43.332
Sorry.

34:43.415 --> 34:45.918
Ms. Pyun, here's my employee ID.

34:46.794 --> 34:48.420
Mr. Baek, can you put the box away?

34:49.046 --> 34:51.924
Goodness. I'm sorry. I apologize.

34:52.007 --> 34:54.176
I'm so sorry.

35:12.569 --> 35:13.987
Mister, you're Moo Kwang-il,
aren't you?

35:14.488 --> 35:16.573
- Yes, who are you?
- Don't you know me?

35:17.157 --> 35:18.867
We met at my grandfather's funeral.

35:20.744 --> 35:24.081
Yes, you're Ms. Eom's eldest son.
It's nice to see you.

35:25.916 --> 35:28.043
I should've known
when you were acting nosy.

35:28.877 --> 35:30.629
Work colleague, my foot.

35:31.171 --> 35:33.048
Who would care
about an outsourced worker's family?

35:33.132 --> 35:34.133
You were coming onto her!

35:35.259 --> 35:38.220
There must be
a huge misunderstanding.

35:38.303 --> 35:40.597
A misunderstanding?
That's easy for you to say.

35:41.098 --> 35:43.475
My mom lost her job
and can't make a living anymore!

35:43.851 --> 35:45.936
You'll probably be fine
because you're a big corporate guy

35:46.520 --> 35:48.522
but my mom is an expendable! Get it?

35:48.605 --> 35:50.023
Let go of me!

35:50.315 --> 35:51.817
- Sir.
- Goodness!

35:51.900 --> 35:53.735
Did she seem that easy to you,
you punk?

35:54.403 --> 35:56.447
- Hey, goodness. Wait a second.
- Let go of me!

35:56.905 --> 35:58.073
Let go!

35:58.157 --> 35:59.450
- You can't do this here.
- Let go!

36:00.826 --> 36:02.995
You went around acting nosy
like you were my dad. This is great.

36:03.078 --> 36:05.831
You can now be my dad
and make a living for me, okay?

36:05.914 --> 36:08.125
Dad... Father...

36:08.208 --> 36:09.251
- Sir.
- Darn it.

36:12.504 --> 36:14.339
Will you let go of me?

36:14.590 --> 36:16.091
Just let go!

36:16.175 --> 36:17.551
Please calm down.

36:18.427 --> 36:19.470
Let go of me!

36:20.220 --> 36:22.306
How dare you hit on my poor mother?

36:22.389 --> 36:24.683
How can you be so vulgar
at your age? Darn it!

36:24.766 --> 36:27.144
I knew he was like that
when he acted too nice.

36:46.538 --> 36:49.124
It was a temporary reaction
due to stress

36:49.208 --> 36:50.751
so please get a good rest.

36:51.543 --> 36:53.962
Would you like anything to eat?

37:01.136 --> 37:02.763
Come on, let's leave.
Get a good rest.

37:05.307 --> 37:07.601
I've never seen Mr. Moo
look so disheartened before.

37:07.851 --> 37:09.686
He must feel awful.

37:10.395 --> 37:13.357
People took his act of kindness
and called it an affair and whatnot.

37:13.440 --> 37:15.526
They all blamed him
like they were hunting him down.

37:15.609 --> 37:17.277
It is too petty a matter
to even make excuses for.

37:17.694 --> 37:19.530
Jeez, this is awful.

37:20.280 --> 37:22.115
The bulletin has become crazier
in the meantime.

37:22.866 --> 37:25.118
"No one is kind enough to visit
the cafeteria lady's dad's funeral."

37:25.410 --> 37:26.703
They say it's 100 percent an affair.

37:26.787 --> 37:28.664
Man, that's just too much.

37:29.039 --> 37:31.041
Why are people like this? Why?

37:32.501 --> 37:33.710
- Hello.
- Hello.

37:33.794 --> 37:35.504
Is Mr. Moo inside?

37:36.380 --> 37:38.966
- Is he all right?
- What do you think?

37:39.550 --> 37:41.260
- Do you have the result?
- Yes.

37:41.343 --> 37:43.220
It doesn't seem like
they were having an affair

37:44.054 --> 37:46.390
but Mr. Moo will be reprimanded...

37:46.473 --> 37:48.350
If he didn't have an affair,
why should he be?

37:48.433 --> 37:50.269
After all, there was a commotion
within the company

37:50.352 --> 37:52.729
and our reputation fell
when the word got out, so...

37:52.813 --> 37:54.648
How is that his fault?

37:54.731 --> 37:57.359
- He's the victim of a witch hunt!
- Yes.

37:57.442 --> 38:00.279
I agree with you, but it's Ms. Joo.

38:01.196 --> 38:02.864
- Excuse me.
- Wait a second.

38:03.365 --> 38:05.367
Mr. Moo can't afford
to be shocked anymore right now.

38:06.118 --> 38:07.202
Also, we cannot accept

38:07.828 --> 38:09.413
this disciplinary action.

38:09.997 --> 38:11.665
How will that change anything?

38:12.165 --> 38:15.419
Let's go and ask Ms. Joo
to withdraw this as a team.

38:16.837 --> 38:18.839
Yes, it's time to protest.

38:20.841 --> 38:23.635
Well, the thing is...
It's embarrassing to bring this up.

38:24.386 --> 38:27.514
I lost my fortune in crypto before
and couldn't pay my credit card bill

38:27.598 --> 38:28.640
but Mr. Moo helped me out.

38:29.057 --> 38:33.061
And she should do her part as a boss
to cover for her team in these times.

38:33.145 --> 38:35.564
I wonder if she'd do that
when I do something wrong

38:35.647 --> 38:37.399
- so it feels very personal.
- You're right.

38:37.941 --> 38:39.401
This isn't just Mr. Moo's business.

38:39.484 --> 38:41.361
This is everyone's problem.

38:41.445 --> 38:44.865
Things seem
a bit heated up right now.

38:45.240 --> 38:47.159
Why don't we calm down
and use our common sense to think...

38:47.242 --> 38:48.910
Do you want to stay out of this?

38:49.786 --> 38:53.332
Why? Do you not want to take part
because you're the Audit Team's ace?

39:04.676 --> 39:06.678
COME TO THE ROOFTOP! PLEASE
FROM AUDIT TEAM 3

39:50.764 --> 39:52.224
It was a phrase
I haven't heard for a while.

39:52.307 --> 39:53.725
"Come to the rooftop."

39:55.227 --> 39:56.603
So are you ganging up on me?

39:57.396 --> 39:58.814
It's kind of cheap
to outnumber me like this.

39:59.147 --> 40:00.357
Why don't a few of you cross over?

40:06.863 --> 40:07.864
Ms. Joo.

40:08.740 --> 40:10.992
We would like to speak to you
as a team

40:11.493 --> 40:13.412
regarding Mr. Moo.

40:15.956 --> 40:18.625
Withdraw the disciplinary action
against him, please.

40:19.126 --> 40:20.293
- Please do that!
- Please do that!

40:21.253 --> 40:23.922
He's already suffering
from all kinds of malicious rumors.

40:24.005 --> 40:27.592
The notice of his disciplinary action
will only make matters worse.

40:27.968 --> 40:30.595
He wasn't at fault to begin with.
It was a misunderstanding.

41:06.923 --> 41:08.091
Oh, my gosh!

41:17.184 --> 41:18.310
Never mind.

41:19.519 --> 41:20.771
My legs were hurting.

41:26.693 --> 41:28.403
Now, where were we?

41:28.487 --> 41:31.114
Yes, that Mr. Moo
didn't do anything wrong.

41:33.784 --> 41:35.952
You're right.
There was no infidelity between them.

41:36.953 --> 41:40.290
But he took cafeteria food out,
which is considered company property

41:40.373 --> 41:42.000
and exchanged
a considerable amount of money

41:42.083 --> 41:43.210
with an outsourced staff member

41:43.543 --> 41:45.462
causing a controversy
inside and outside the office.

41:46.505 --> 41:47.589
I think

41:48.173 --> 41:49.674
reprimanding him sounds adequate.

41:50.801 --> 41:53.053
Will anyone care
about the whole story?

41:54.012 --> 41:57.265
They'll brand him for infidelity,
thinking the suspicions are right

41:57.766 --> 41:59.184
because of the disciplinary action.

42:02.687 --> 42:05.607
Then will glossing over this matter
put everything to its rest?

42:06.566 --> 42:08.610
"The Audit Team nitpicks over
every little detail with us

42:08.693 --> 42:09.903
but they cover for their own."

42:10.946 --> 42:12.739
Wouldn't people insult
the entire team?

42:12.823 --> 42:15.534
You're our boss
before you're the Head of Audit.

42:16.034 --> 42:18.453
And shouldn't you draw the line
and protect us in times like these

42:18.537 --> 42:20.080
if you truly are our boss?

42:20.664 --> 42:23.625
How can we have faith in this company
if you treat us like this?

42:30.841 --> 42:33.718
You don't need to have faith to work.
We aren't a church.

42:35.220 --> 42:37.973
You come to work
because you get paid to be here!

42:38.682 --> 42:40.976
And because we are paid,
I will fulfill my responsibility

42:41.059 --> 42:43.186
and Mr. Moo must fulfill his own.

42:49.276 --> 42:50.318
"Draw the line"?

42:51.903 --> 42:54.447
That line is there
because you are not to step over it.

43:08.211 --> 43:10.380
White Blood Cell, you're something.

43:10.463 --> 43:12.424
Never mind. Go ahead.

43:13.842 --> 43:15.468
I think we stepped off the deep end.

43:19.014 --> 43:20.557
We can't end it like this.

43:21.391 --> 43:23.018
The negotiation is off

43:24.019 --> 43:25.520
so we must act as a group.

43:25.604 --> 43:28.023
There's no talking to her,
so we must show her with our action.

43:43.872 --> 43:45.165
Excuse me.

43:46.082 --> 43:49.294
Ms. Joo, the entire team
took the rest of the day off.

43:49.836 --> 43:52.547
They called it a kind of a strike.

43:53.840 --> 43:55.759
They want you to retract
Mr. Moo's disciplinary action.

44:01.723 --> 44:04.601
Goodness. There's a fly in here.
It's a dung fly.

44:06.895 --> 44:08.855
Is the office not tidy enough?

44:11.942 --> 44:12.943
Sorry?

44:14.611 --> 44:15.654
Yes.

44:17.113 --> 44:18.323
That was it?

44:19.366 --> 44:20.909
All right. Bye.

44:22.661 --> 44:23.828
Why? What did Ms. Joo say?

44:26.456 --> 44:27.666
Nothing.

44:29.668 --> 44:30.919
She caught a fly and turned around.

44:31.002 --> 44:32.295
- That's it?
- Yes.

44:32.379 --> 44:34.005
She must think we're a huge joke.

44:34.089 --> 44:36.299
How can she not respond in any way
even after our group strike?

44:36.383 --> 44:37.884
That's why she's Joo In-a.

44:37.968 --> 44:40.136
I expected this, but how could she
not be bothered at all?

44:40.220 --> 44:41.221
Whatever. Let's keep it going.

44:41.304 --> 44:42.722
Take tomorrow off, too.

44:42.806 --> 44:43.807
Wait a minute.

44:44.641 --> 44:46.643
If Ms. Joo doesn't approve
our leave request

44:46.726 --> 44:48.353
it'll be considered
unauthorized absence.

44:49.854 --> 44:51.064
Wait, in that case...

44:51.398 --> 44:54.234
Is there a possibility
that we'll also get punishment?

44:54.651 --> 44:58.154
Come on.
Ms. Joo can't be that inconsiderate.

44:58.238 --> 45:00.073
Isn't that why we're here now?

45:04.953 --> 45:05.996
In that case

45:06.621 --> 45:09.374
why don't one of us go upstairs
and do a quick vibe check?

45:09.457 --> 45:11.334
And check how Ms. Joo is doing.

45:12.377 --> 45:13.670
Do you want to go, Mr. Noh?

45:14.045 --> 45:15.046
Me?

45:15.130 --> 45:18.341
DOES ANYBODY KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED TO THE MADAM KILLER?

45:19.050 --> 45:20.051
Lastly

45:20.427 --> 45:23.013
Managing Director Jeon Sung-yeol
will return to the headquarters.

45:24.097 --> 45:25.557
I expect you to show him support.

45:36.317 --> 45:37.986
Now it's official.

45:38.069 --> 45:39.487
It must be what the president wants.

45:39.571 --> 45:40.697
Of course, it is.

45:40.780 --> 45:42.949
Jeez, there are two suns
radiating up in our sky.

45:49.914 --> 45:50.999
It'll happen, anyway.

45:57.589 --> 45:58.673
Ms. Boo.

46:03.344 --> 46:04.387
It's Se-young.

46:06.806 --> 46:07.891
Se-young.

46:09.642 --> 46:11.936
Isn't it about time
that you took a measure for Mr. Moo?

46:12.562 --> 46:15.065
HR and Information Office
is in charge of the intranet.

46:15.982 --> 46:17.901
I already shared the result
of our investigation

46:17.984 --> 46:19.527
that the infidelity was groundless.

46:20.612 --> 46:21.905
But the bulletin
is still going strong.

46:21.988 --> 46:23.448
People are like that.

46:24.157 --> 46:25.992
No one cares about the truth.

46:26.076 --> 46:27.160
Exactly.

46:27.786 --> 46:30.205
So I'm asking HR
to delete those posts accordingly.

46:33.208 --> 46:34.751
We've been a little busy.

46:35.877 --> 46:36.961
I'll look into it, though.

46:38.213 --> 46:39.756
It's because of Mr. Jeon, isn't it?

46:42.550 --> 46:44.260
The bulletin always has
posts about him

46:44.344 --> 46:46.179
so you're diverting people
and manipulating opinions.

46:47.305 --> 46:49.099
I've noticed it a while ago

46:49.182 --> 46:50.683
but HR was doing what HR does

46:51.142 --> 46:52.602
so I was going to observe.

46:53.394 --> 46:54.437
But you know

46:55.688 --> 46:57.524
I've had enough of your nonsense.

46:57.899 --> 46:58.942
Nonsense?

46:59.692 --> 47:02.654
Hey. Do you think HR is a joke?

47:06.658 --> 47:07.700
Anyway.

47:08.284 --> 47:10.328
But in the end,
I guess I have to thank him.

47:11.037 --> 47:13.414
You always cover up a rumor
with another rumor.

47:15.542 --> 47:16.584
Right?

47:17.502 --> 47:20.171
You cover up a rumor
with another rumor, right?

47:28.638 --> 47:31.641
What are you doing?
Hey. Let go of me. Hey!

47:31.724 --> 47:32.809
You!

47:33.309 --> 47:36.146
Have you lost your mind?
Get over here.

47:36.563 --> 47:38.606
Let go of me!

47:38.690 --> 47:40.775
Let go! Hey!

47:41.359 --> 47:44.320
Let go! Let go of my hair!

47:44.404 --> 47:46.447
Have you lost your mind?

47:46.531 --> 47:48.449
Hey! Let go of me!

47:52.996 --> 47:55.248
Let go of my hair!

47:55.331 --> 47:56.833
'22 RECRUITS GROUP CHAT
1 NEW MESSAGE

47:56.916 --> 47:59.002
AUDIT TEAM 3 GROUP CHAT
1 NEW MESSAGE

48:00.211 --> 48:02.046
You. Let go of me.

48:02.380 --> 48:03.631
Let go!

48:21.024 --> 48:22.066
What kind of person

48:22.775 --> 48:24.319
is Joo In-a?

48:30.658 --> 48:32.202
- No way.
- This is the craziest ever.

48:32.285 --> 48:34.662
- People made so many clips.
- Why did they fight?

48:34.746 --> 48:35.830
They've always been enemies.

48:36.539 --> 48:37.582
Everyone knew.

48:39.876 --> 48:42.086
In the end, did everything go
according to her plan?

48:42.629 --> 48:43.671
Right?

48:43.880 --> 48:46.382
You cover up a rumor
with another rumor, right?

48:58.269 --> 48:59.354
Know your limits.

48:59.646 --> 49:02.190
A cornered mouse can bite the cat.

49:14.160 --> 49:15.203
Ms. Joo.

49:15.745 --> 49:16.955
I need to talk to you.

49:19.249 --> 49:21.376
Unfortunately, I'm done for the day.

49:21.918 --> 49:23.419
Please come to my office tomorrow.

49:24.921 --> 49:26.089
What the heck is this complaint?

49:26.172 --> 49:28.132
Wasn't the disciplinary action
more than enough?

49:28.591 --> 49:30.260
Are you trying

49:30.760 --> 49:32.971
to end someone's life?

49:34.180 --> 49:35.306
Let's talk.

50:08.423 --> 50:09.465
Anyway, Ms. Joo.

50:11.009 --> 50:12.302
Do you have to keep

50:13.594 --> 50:15.138
the rest of your fingers folded in?

50:18.850 --> 50:20.143
I wanted to make it easier for you.

50:22.103 --> 50:23.146
Right.

50:24.605 --> 50:26.691
Goodness. Of all those fingers,
you hurt this one.

50:36.534 --> 50:37.577
All done.

50:38.369 --> 50:41.080
I only gave you first aid,
so please see a doctor tomorrow.

50:41.164 --> 50:43.791
Okay. You're my savior today, so...

50:45.418 --> 50:47.295
Please enjoy, sir.

50:52.175 --> 50:53.968
Is this what your life is worth?

50:54.052 --> 50:55.845
It's not for my life.
It's for my finger.

50:57.347 --> 50:59.057
I look stylish and powerful.

50:59.557 --> 51:00.600
I like this one.

51:01.559 --> 51:02.643
"This one"?

51:03.061 --> 51:04.395
Does this happen to you often?

51:04.479 --> 51:05.980
This is kind of cute, actually.

51:06.814 --> 51:08.816
Back in the day,
someone destroyed my computer

51:08.900 --> 51:11.402
and another employee fled after
splashing my seat with superglue.

51:11.736 --> 51:13.905
And a CEO of a corrupt business
struck my head with a golf club.

51:14.405 --> 51:15.490
I probably have a scar here.

51:15.573 --> 51:17.617
Right here. Can you see it?

51:18.117 --> 51:19.202
It's from my surgery back then.

51:19.869 --> 51:21.120
While I was working abroad

51:21.204 --> 51:23.373
the local gang
even threatened me with a knife.

51:24.415 --> 51:25.500
So I

51:26.459 --> 51:27.543
picked up a gun.

51:32.924 --> 51:34.384
That's why you're Joo-niper.

51:35.176 --> 51:37.637
So that rumor was true?
Did you really shoot a person?

51:38.262 --> 51:39.389
What do you think?

51:42.850 --> 51:44.102
No, I don't want to know.

51:54.153 --> 51:55.196
Ms. Joo.

51:56.906 --> 51:58.866
About your fight with the Head of HR.

52:04.664 --> 52:05.706
No, never mind.

52:12.213 --> 52:13.423
Are you perverted?

52:14.090 --> 52:16.551
- What?
- Do you get off on getting hated?

52:17.093 --> 52:19.303
I know it's hard not to make enemies
when you're working

52:19.387 --> 52:20.847
but you can try to make less.

52:21.556 --> 52:22.849
But it seems like

52:23.850 --> 52:25.518
you want to get hated

52:25.852 --> 52:26.978
even more than you actually want.

52:29.480 --> 52:31.399
No one wants to be hated.

52:32.191 --> 52:34.986
However, there are times
when I must position myself.

52:35.611 --> 52:37.655
I must either be a saint
or a villain.

52:38.489 --> 52:40.074
If I stay in the middle,
I get no work done

52:40.158 --> 52:42.368
lose my popularity,
and nothing works out.

52:43.494 --> 52:45.121
Do you know who your worst boss is?

52:46.914 --> 52:47.999
A non-committal jerk.

52:50.251 --> 52:51.294
Yes.

52:51.544 --> 52:53.212
You definitely are committed to one.

53:02.472 --> 53:03.639
But it must be lonely

53:05.475 --> 53:06.809
to have your sincerity misunderstood.

53:11.939 --> 53:13.274
Did you misunderstand me?

53:13.816 --> 53:14.859
How so?

53:18.529 --> 53:20.031
That you were a cold-hearted person

53:20.114 --> 53:23.826
who don't care about others' feelings
to accomplish your goals.

53:26.412 --> 53:27.580
Well, I thought so.

53:29.665 --> 53:31.709
But you seem to be someone
who does things your own way

53:32.877 --> 53:34.712
when you do something
you believe is right.

53:37.465 --> 53:39.717
People may misunderstand you
because of that

53:40.510 --> 53:42.136
and you put yourself
in a hard position

53:42.803 --> 53:43.930
but you do not back out

53:44.680 --> 53:45.765
or make excuses.

53:47.975 --> 53:49.227
I doubt it's easy

53:51.229 --> 53:52.355
to always live like that.

54:01.405 --> 54:02.448
Wow.

54:03.115 --> 54:04.700
You know how to talk, Mr. Noh.

54:05.660 --> 54:07.036
I was a bit moved just now.

54:10.331 --> 54:13.376
Anyway, don't you think
the misunderstanding was harsh?

54:13.793 --> 54:15.378
You practically thought
I was a psychopath.

54:15.461 --> 54:17.088
You do come across that way.

54:17.672 --> 54:18.839
Me?

54:18.923 --> 54:20.591
But I love people.

54:20.883 --> 54:22.426
Even personality tests say
I'm an extrovert

54:22.510 --> 54:24.262
- like a cute little puppy.
- Cute little puppy?

54:24.762 --> 54:27.390
People are intimidated by you!

54:30.309 --> 54:31.394
You can't have this.

54:32.395 --> 54:34.188
Look at this.

54:34.272 --> 54:36.232
This is why you come off like that.

54:36.816 --> 54:38.150
Give it back.

54:38.734 --> 54:41.195
I'm a big psychopath,
so I can't do that.

54:45.491 --> 54:47.285
It's even better
because I took it back from you.

54:48.119 --> 54:49.328
Don't finish it. It's mine...

54:58.963 --> 55:00.798
You skipped dinner today.

55:01.507 --> 55:02.883
You should eat,
even if you don't want to.

55:03.301 --> 55:05.011
Okay. Leave it there and go.

55:12.351 --> 55:13.853
It's the key to the studio apartment.

55:15.229 --> 55:16.772
Thank you for everything.

55:18.107 --> 55:19.400
While moving out

55:19.650 --> 55:22.194
I stole a bottle of your hard liquor
as a souvenir.

55:23.154 --> 55:24.155
Is that okay?

55:27.783 --> 55:29.076
I don't mind.

55:30.661 --> 55:31.704
But why the sudden change?

55:32.580 --> 55:34.790
Has your family matter been resolved?

55:35.207 --> 55:36.292
No.

55:37.043 --> 55:38.044
I just

55:40.087 --> 55:41.922
don't want to stay there anymore.

55:44.342 --> 55:45.676
Then where are you staying?

55:46.886 --> 55:48.929
- Is it safe?
- I'm not telling.

55:50.556 --> 55:52.808
I want you to be concerned

55:53.934 --> 55:54.977
about me.

56:25.925 --> 56:27.301
He wrapped it up so neatly.

57:30.906 --> 57:31.907
Jae-yeol!

57:52.303 --> 57:53.471
I'll see you more often now.

57:54.054 --> 57:55.097
Jae-yeol.

57:56.432 --> 57:57.475
Sure.

58:02.772 --> 58:04.565
It's been a while
since I've written an apology

58:04.648 --> 58:06.150
and I found the fun in it.

58:12.865 --> 58:14.658
- Mr. Moo.
- Yes?

58:14.742 --> 58:16.452
You're a special man who have worked

58:16.535 --> 58:18.829
in 12 teams, 5 branches,
and 3 different subsidiaries.

58:19.830 --> 58:21.749
You're highly interested
in every aspect of the company

58:21.832 --> 58:23.334
so you have information and network.

58:24.376 --> 58:26.462
It makes you a perfect candidate
to take up Audit Team Three

58:26.545 --> 58:28.339
a team that receives
dozens of complains a day.

58:29.298 --> 58:30.299
Above all

58:30.674 --> 58:32.510
you're a good leader
to your team members

58:32.760 --> 58:34.637
who each have a big personality.

58:34.929 --> 58:38.432
Goodness, I appreciate
your words of consolation.

58:38.516 --> 58:39.517
However

58:40.476 --> 58:41.644
that's a double-edged sword.

58:42.228 --> 58:44.063
Your sound personality

58:44.146 --> 58:46.440
sometimes doesn't fit
to be the leader of the Audit Team.

58:47.233 --> 58:49.568
Members of other departments are
the subjects of our investigation.

58:50.319 --> 58:51.821
Make use of them as your intel

58:51.904 --> 58:53.948
but please try to keep them
in a proper distance.

58:56.742 --> 58:58.869
How can I make use of people
as my intel?

58:58.953 --> 59:00.037
I'm not a spy.

59:01.747 --> 59:02.790
Goodness.

59:03.582 --> 59:04.625
Well, Ms. Joo.

59:05.125 --> 59:06.919
I crunched some numbers

59:08.045 --> 59:10.923
and realized that during weekdays,
I can only play with my daughters

59:11.006 --> 59:12.550
two hours a day at most.

59:13.217 --> 59:15.719
But I must sit here
and work with my colleagues

59:15.803 --> 59:17.805
for nine hours a day.

59:18.597 --> 59:19.807
And in those hours

59:20.057 --> 59:21.851
if I do not keep
a friendly relationship

59:22.142 --> 59:23.769
with my colleagues

59:24.436 --> 59:25.771
it would make my life

59:27.648 --> 59:28.983
too meaningless.

59:30.025 --> 59:31.026
In the future

59:31.610 --> 59:34.905
I will do my best to help out
if I find another colleague in need

59:35.447 --> 59:38.742
and gladly take any food they bring
if they decide to do that.

59:39.368 --> 59:41.036
I'll write up another apology
when that happens.

59:43.622 --> 59:44.665
I'm sorry.

59:45.958 --> 59:48.961
Anyway, I will do my job
without a big ambition

59:49.336 --> 59:52.464
but for a long time
while enjoying my time here.

59:59.221 --> 01:00:01.932
If you have nothing more to say,
then please excuse me.

01:00:03.309 --> 01:00:04.351
All right.

01:00:07.354 --> 01:00:08.564
Oh, Ms. Joo.

01:00:11.108 --> 01:00:14.862
By any chance,
did you pull out Ms. Boo's hair

01:00:15.654 --> 01:00:17.531
for my sake?

01:00:18.866 --> 01:00:20.159
Is that important?

01:00:21.201 --> 01:00:23.329
No. Please excuse me.

01:00:32.379 --> 01:00:33.422
Perhaps

01:00:34.506 --> 01:00:36.800
distinguishing between
your friend and foe at work

01:00:43.015 --> 01:00:44.934
is not that important.

01:00:49.438 --> 01:00:50.564
I don't work here anymore.

01:00:51.815 --> 01:00:54.068
I got a better job elsewhere,
so don't worry about me.

01:00:54.360 --> 01:00:56.236
Goodness,
you're such a talented person.

01:00:56.320 --> 01:00:57.363
Good for you.

01:00:59.323 --> 01:01:01.992
Please give me a call
when your twins get married.

01:01:02.451 --> 01:01:03.953
I may not give you as much

01:01:04.036 --> 01:01:05.537
but I want to show you
my token of sincerity.

01:01:05.621 --> 01:01:06.664
Of course.

01:01:11.251 --> 01:01:12.628
- Stay healthy.
- Thank you.

01:01:13.003 --> 01:01:14.171
Thank you for your hard work.

01:01:20.219 --> 01:01:21.595
What's more important is...

01:01:22.763 --> 01:01:26.767
HEAD OF AUDIT

01:01:26.850 --> 01:01:29.269
Gosh, the air in this office
is way too dry.

01:01:29.353 --> 01:01:31.313
I should tidy this up a little.

01:01:33.565 --> 01:01:35.526
Are you done?
Ms. Joo, here's your coffee.

01:01:35.943 --> 01:01:37.111
Goodness.

01:01:40.572 --> 01:01:41.907
Let me dry that off.

01:01:48.372 --> 01:01:50.916
Shoo!

01:01:52.835 --> 01:01:54.795
Shoo.

01:01:56.964 --> 01:01:58.048
Excuse us.

01:02:01.719 --> 01:02:03.804
...the discretion
not to turn your friend into a foe.

01:02:04.805 --> 01:02:06.390
By any chance, do you feel hot?

01:02:06.473 --> 01:02:07.808
Should I fan you?

01:02:07.891 --> 01:02:09.435
- Stronger.
- Stronger wind.

01:02:10.686 --> 01:02:11.812
Does that feel better?

01:02:23.574 --> 01:02:26.368
And the determination to gladly
become my colleague's friend.

01:02:27.786 --> 01:02:28.996
Perhaps those are more important.

01:02:47.222 --> 01:02:48.515
RECREATIONAL ART CLASS
TONIGHT AT 9 P.M.

01:02:52.436 --> 01:02:55.189
Even someone who has
a great reputation like Mr. Moo

01:02:56.065 --> 01:02:58.150
got cornered
because of a single photo.

01:03:00.194 --> 01:03:01.695
Joo In-a has enemies all around her.

01:03:06.241 --> 01:03:07.284
That report.

01:03:07.493 --> 01:03:09.036
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

01:03:09.119 --> 01:03:10.496
It's probably
an attempt to entrap her.

01:03:11.538 --> 01:03:13.624
All right. I need to stop here.

01:03:48.033 --> 01:03:49.243
Wait. Excuse me.

01:03:50.911 --> 01:03:52.871
Do you need that
to take a class here?

01:03:53.122 --> 01:03:54.456
Oh, yes.

01:03:55.249 --> 01:03:57.626
The club members must bring it.

01:03:57.876 --> 01:03:59.837
I see. Thank you.

01:04:07.719 --> 01:04:08.762
What's going on?

01:04:09.721 --> 01:04:11.181
She wasn't carrying that thing.

01:06:12.636 --> 01:06:15.555
FILING FOR LOVE

01:06:16.014 --> 01:06:18.934
GUEST APPEARANCE BY LEE JUNG-EUN

01:06:44.584 --> 01:06:45.711
How can I act like nothing happened?

01:06:45.794 --> 01:06:46.795
It's just not the same.

01:06:48.005 --> 01:06:49.172
This is driving me crazy.

01:06:49.256 --> 01:06:51.717
Babe, come here. Hurry.

01:06:52.342 --> 01:06:53.635
- Bravo!
- There's

01:06:53.719 --> 01:06:55.220
definitely more to this incident.

01:06:55.304 --> 01:06:57.931
Who did you mess with

01:06:58.015 --> 01:06:59.182
to become their target?

01:06:59.266 --> 01:07:00.767
If this backfires
due to a careless move

01:07:00.851 --> 01:07:02.060
you could be in serious trouble.

01:07:02.144 --> 01:07:03.270
I'll make sure it doesn't backfire.

01:07:03.353 --> 01:07:04.479
Room 1306, please.

01:07:04.563 --> 01:07:05.897
I'm staying the night.

01:07:05.981 --> 01:07:08.483
Why are you hesitating now?
You've already seen it.

01:07:09.860 --> 01:07:11.820
- Could you stop staring at my body?
- Sorry?

01:07:25.709 --> 01:07:27.711
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
